Md. Omar Faruk, AI and machine learning engineer.

4
00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.510
Md. Abdur Rahman, full-stack and backend.

5
00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:14.920
Mohammed Mahmud Parvez, full-stack developer.

6
00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:17.980
Md. Morsalin, full-stack and backend.

7
00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:20.240
And our advisor, Md Rifat,

8
00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:22.990
domain and network expert, joining us online.

9
00:00:23.608 --> 00:00:27.568
In Bangladesh, a potato farmer often sells below cost.

10
00:00:27.568 --> 00:00:30.410
Between the field and the buyer, five tiers of middlemen

11
00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:34.478
can mark the price up by as much as 116%.

12
00:00:34.478 --> 00:00:37.928
Traders hold 77% of the cold-storage space,

13
00:00:37.928 --> 00:00:41.478
and a single flash flood can wipe out an entire season.

14
00:00:41.684 --> 00:00:44.776
KrishiNexus OS is one AI operating system

15
00:00:44.776 --> 00:00:46.734
for everyone in that chain:

16
00:00:46.734 --> 00:00:49.454
the farmer, the co-op, the cold store,

17
00:00:49.454 --> 00:00:52.274
the buyer, the truck driver and the bank.

18
00:00:52.274 --> 00:00:54.834
Each one signs in to their own workspace.

19
00:00:55.049 --> 00:00:57.499
Rahim is a potato farmer in Rangpur.

20
00:00:57.499 --> 00:00:59.419
He simply asks in his own dialect.

21
00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:03.399
After he gives consent, four AI agents grade his crop,

22
00:01:03.709 --> 00:01:07.049
compare today's market with cold storage and a shared truck,

23
00:01:07.049 --> 00:01:08.679
and check the flood risk.

24
00:01:08.679 --> 00:01:11.989
A circuit breaker stops him from selling below his cost,

25
00:01:11.989 --> 00:01:13.499
and it shows its working.

26
00:01:13.731 --> 00:01:15.841
He can also photograph his potatoes.

27
00:01:15.841 --> 00:01:18.991
A trained vision model finds every tuber and its defects,

28
00:01:19.311 --> 00:01:21.181
then signs a quality certificate.

29
00:01:21.501 --> 00:01:24.731
Buyers and banks can verify that certificate for themselves.

30
00:01:24.941 --> 00:01:28.001
Behind every answer, you can watch the agents work.

31
00:01:28.351 --> 00:01:30.421
They retrieve Bangladeshi farm data,

32
00:01:30.421 --> 00:01:33.181
call live tools through three MCP servers,

33
00:01:33.181 --> 00:01:35.101
and every step is traced.

34
00:01:35.101 --> 00:01:36.055
It even runs offline,

35
00:01:36.055 --> 00:01:39.411
on a fine-tuned Bangla model at a village kiosk.

36
00:01:39.716 --> 00:01:43.036
Co-ops pool small harvests into full five-ton trucks.

37
00:01:43.466 --> 00:01:46.796
The cold store sees live chamber sensors in a 3D twin.

38
00:01:46.796 --> 00:01:50.476
And when a flood or heat alert arrives, the trucks are rerouted.

39
00:01:50.666 --> 00:01:52.236
Rahim can also sell directly.

40
00:01:52.596 --> 00:01:55.046
He lists his lot, traders bid in the open,

41
00:01:55.586 --> 00:01:57.326
and he accepts the best bid.

42
00:01:57.326 --> 00:01:59.146
The payment is held in escrow.

43
00:01:59.146 --> 00:02:00.232
A driver takes the job

44
00:02:00.232 --> 00:02:03.046
and reports the load temperature along the road.

45
00:02:03.046 --> 00:02:06.446
Our shelf-life model checks that the potatoes will arrive safe,

46
00:02:06.446 --> 00:02:09.406
and on delivery the payment is released to Rahim.

47
00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:13.620
Banks see a credit score from 300 to 850.

48
00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:16.570
It is backed by satellite flood checks and signed certificates.

49
00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:20.170
So a farmer without collateral can still get credit.

50
00:02:20.519 --> 00:02:23.529
We trained five models, and we publish every score,

51
00:02:23.529 --> 00:02:25.979
including the ones that missed their targets.

52
00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:30.119
The app asks for consent. It removes names and phone numbers.

53
00:02:30.119 --> 00:02:32.419
It keeps data for 24 hours only,

54
00:02:32.419 --> 00:02:35.769
and it always leaves the final decision to the farmer.

55
00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:39.850
KrishiNexus also fits in a farmer's pocket.

56
00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:42.250
Our Android app speaks Bangla:

57
00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:44.670
Rahim asks out loud and hears the answer back.

58
00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:48.800
He photographs his harvest and gets a signed grade in seconds.

59
00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:52.840
Buyers bid from their phones, drivers share their live location,

60
00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:55.170
and everyone follows the sale in real time.

61
00:02:58.989 --> 00:03:00.959
One pooled truck covers its costs.

62
00:03:01.349 --> 00:03:04.119
A district breaks even at 16 trucks a month.

63
00:03:04.119 --> 00:03:05.661
We start a field test this December

64
00:03:05.661 --> 00:03:08.129
and a potato pilot in January.

65
00:03:08.129 --> 00:03:11.359
This is KrishiNexus OS, by Team Heat Wave.

66
00:03:11.359 --> 00:03:13.207
Try it now at tanvir.health.
